ex:TwentysixGasolineStations
        rdf:type                    ex:ArtistBook , ex:ArtistsBook , ex:Book;
        ex:createdBy                "Ed Ruscha";
        ex:describedAs              "1 volume : (chiefly illustrations) ; 18 cm.";
        ex:editionYear              "1969";
        ex:hasDescription           "Largely considered the first modern artists' book, TwentySix Gasoline Stations is also the first bookwork by Ed Ruscha. Self-published in 1963 and in second and third editions in 1967 and 1969, Twentysix Gasoline Stations features black-and-white photos of gas stations taken from a distance along Route 66 in Southern California, Arizona, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and Texas, documenting the modernization of the American landscape and its expanding network of highways.--Printed Matter website.";
